        <item>
            <title>2.0.11</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:29:57 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20011</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.11</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Proximity now scales each layer by a share of its own size. Images from Figma, which arrive scaled down, grow as much as every other layer, and mirrored layers no longer shrink when they should grow. Layers at 100 % behave exactly as before. To update layers you already set up, apply Proximity to them again.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Also new since 2.0.9</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Images from Figma arrive as the image itself, scaled to its Figma size, so Grid Builder, 3D and motion blur work on them right away. Precomp next to Layer keeps the previous way, and the menu next to Layer sets the resolution: Auto, or 1x to 5x.</li>
  <li>Convert selected in the Rectangle section turns rectangles you already have into MotionUI rectangles without changing their look.</li>
  <li>License and App updates come first in Settings. The version number opens Settings, and a small badge next to it installs a downloaded update. Settings is also in the MotionUI menu on a Mac (⌘,) and in the tray menu on Windows.</li>
  <li>When another program holds the Figma link, MotionUI names it. On Windows, MotionUI starts with Windows, and screen readers read the tabs and switches.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
