        <item>
            <title>2.0.10</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:04:25 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>20010</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.10</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>MotionUI 2.0.10</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Images from Figma now arrive as the image itself, scaled to its Figma size, so Grid Builder, 3D and motion blur work on them right away. Choose Precomp next to Layer to keep the previous way. The menu next to Layer sets the resolution: Auto, or 1x to 5x for every image when you want to zoom in close.</li>
  <li>Convert selected in the Rectangle section turns rectangles you already have, drawn in After Effects or imported, into MotionUI rectangles. The look stays the same, and width, height and corners become sliders you can animate.</li>
  <li>Settings are easier to find: License and App updates come first, the version number in the header opens Settings, and a small badge next to it shows a downloaded update. Click the badge to install it. On a Mac, Settings is also in the MotionUI menu (⌘,); on Windows, in the menu of the tray icon.</li>
  <li>When another program holds the Figma link, MotionUI now names it, for example MotionUI Dev. On a Mac you can quit it right there.</li>
  <li>On Windows, MotionUI starts with Windows, so Figma stays linked and updates arrive after a restart. You can turn this off in Settings. Screen readers now read the tabs and switches of the window.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
